<title>UK: UK retail prices up yr/yr 2.7 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>UK retail prices up yr/yr 2.7 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following retail price indices for October:</p>
<p>    RETAIL PRICES INDEX	   OCT	  SEPT	OCT 95</p>
<p>    Mthly RPI pct change	  UNCH	 0.5	-0.5</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr RPI pct change     2.7	  2.1	 3.2</p>
<p>    RPI Index (base Jan 1987)   153.8	153.8     149.8</p>
<p>    Mth change minus mortgages  UNCH	 0.5	-0.3</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr minus mortgages    3.3*	 2.9	 2.9</p>
<p>    Index minus mortgages	 153.6	153.6     148.7</p>
<p>    Mth pct change ex MIPs, tax UNCH	 0.6	-0.4</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr change ex MIPs,tax 3.0	  2.5	 2.4</p>
<p>    Index ex MIPS, indirect tax 149.6	149.6     145.3</p>
<p>COMPONENT DETAILS OF THE ALL-ITEMS INDEX (PCT CHANGES) -</p>
<p>				    OCT     YR/YR	SEPT    YR/YR</p>
<p>  Food			    -0.8    2.0	 -1.0	1.7</p>
<p>    seasonal food	     -4.0   -6.2	 -5.8     -9.7</p>
<p>    non-seasonal food	 -0.3    3.4	 -0.2	3.9</p>
<p>  Catering			 0.2    4.0	  0.3	4.2</p>
<p>  Alcoholic drink		0.2    2.5	  0.1	2.8</p>
<p>  Tobacco			  0.1    7.1	  0.2	6.9</p>
<p>  Housing			  0.2    1.5	 -0.1	0.1</p>
<p>  Fuel and light		-0.1    0.1	  UNCH     0.2</p>
<p>  Household goods	     -0.4    2.3	  0.5	2.5</p>
<p>  Household services	  -0.5    1.0	  0.6	1.2</p>
<p>  Clothing and footwear     UNCH   -0.1	  5.2     -0.2</p>
<p>  Personal goods &amp; services  0.7    3.6	  0.5	3.3</p>
<p>  Motoring expenditure	 0.6    6.4	  1.5	4.4</p>
<p>  Fares &amp; travel costs	-0.1    3.8	  0.2	3.6</p>
<p>  Leisure goods		 -0.2    1.1	  UNCH     1.6</p>
<p>  Leisure services	     0.4    3.5	  0.5	3.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was RPI -0.2 pct MM,+2.5 pct YY, RPIX +3.1 pct YY, RPIY +2.8 pct YY.  </p>
<p>(MIPS=mortgage interest payments)</p>
<p>The ONS said the rise in the 12-month rate was largely attributable to housing and motoring costs, though there were also smaller upward effects from food prices and charges for leisure services.</p>
<p>The ONS said slight downward effects on the 12-month rate came from price changes for alcoholic drink, household goods and leisure goods.</p>
<p>The tax and price index was 143.0 in October, unchanged from September and up 1.3 percent on the year.</p>
<p>*Highest rate since September 1993</p>
</text>
